The easiest way to build this package is with the bpkg package manager:

$ bpkg build libstudxml

But if you don't want to use the package manager, then you can also build it
manually using the standard build2 build system.

On Linux, an alternative CMake build uses system Expat (2.1 or later) and
requires a C++11 compiler:

$ cmake -S . -B cmake-build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr
$ cmake --build cmake-build
$ cmake --install cmake-build

This builds a shared library with the private Genx implementation and
installs headers and libstudxml.pc for pkg-config consumers.
